hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"20601","Waki' narrated to us, Abd al-Majid Abu Amr narrated to me, al-Ad-da' ibn Khalid ibn Hawdhah narrated to me, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressing the people on the Day of Arafah on a camel, standing in the stirrups."
"20602","Yunus narrated to us, Umar ibn Ibrahim al-Yashkuri narrated to us, a great old shaykh from Banu Uqayl called Abd al-Majid al-Uqayli narrated to us, he said: We set out as pilgrims on the nights Yazid ibn al-Muhallab revolted, and it had been mentioned to us that there was a water in al-Aliyah called al-Zujayj. When we completed our rites we came until we reached al-Zujayj and made our mounts kneel. He said: Then we went on until we came to a well over which were old henna-dyed men talking. He said: We said: This one who accompanied the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), where is his house? They said: Yes, he accompanied him, and that is his house. So we went on until we came to the house and greeted. He said: He gave us permission, and there he was, a great old shaykh lying down, called al-Ad-da' ibn Khalid al-Kilabi. I said: Are you the one who accompanied the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes, and were it not that it is night I would have read to you the letter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to me. He said: Who are you? We said: From the people of Basrah. He said: Welcome to you. What has Yazid ibn al-Muhallab done? We said: He is there calling to the Book of Allah, Blessed and Exalted, and to the Sunnah of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: What has he to do with that, what has he to do with that. He said: I said: Which shall we follow, these or these, meaning the people of Sham or Yazid? He said: If you sit back you will prosper and be rightly guided, if you sit back you will prosper and be rightly guided, I do not know it except that he said it three times. I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the Day of Arafah standing in the stirrups calling out at the top of his voice: O people, what day is this day of yours? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: What month is this month of yours? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: What land is this land of yours? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: Your day is a sacred day, your month is a sacred month, and your land is a sacred land. He said: Then he said: Verily your blood and your wealth are sacred to you as the sanctity of this day of yours in this month of yours in this land of yours until the Day you meet your Lord, Blessed and Exalted, and He will ask you about your deeds. He said: Then he raised his hands to the sky and said: O Allah, bear witness over them, O Allah, bear witness over them, he mentioned it repeatedly and I do not know how many times he mentioned it."
